</think>For a stationary \(\pi^+\) decay:

\[
\pi^+ \to \mu^+ + \nu
\]

Using energy and momentum conservation with \(m_\nu \approx 0\):

\[
E_\mu = \frac{m_\pi^2 + m_\mu^2}{2m_\pi}
\]

\[
E_\mu = \frac{139.6^2 + 105.7^2}{2(139.6)}
= 109.816 \text{ MeV}
\]

So,

\[
KE_\mu = E_\mu - m_\mu = 109.816 - 105.7 = 4.116 \approx 4.12 \text{ MeV}
\]

The neutrino energy is:

\[
E_\nu = m_\pi - E_\mu = 139.6 - 109.816 = 29.784 \approx 29.8 \text{ MeV}
\]

Thus the kinetic energies are approximately:

\[
4.12 \text{ MeV},\ 29.8 \text{ MeV}
\]

Answer: B
