Let's craft final with equations. Desired oververbosity 5. Need not too long. Final line exactly "Answer: C". Ensure nothing after.</think>For an eclipsing double-lined spectroscopic binary, assuming edge-on orbits, the total mass scales as:

\[
M_{\rm total} \propto P (K_1+K_2)^3
\]

System 1:
\[
P_1=2\ \text{yr},\quad K_1+K_2=10+5=15\ \text{km/s}
\]

System 2:
\[
P_2=1\ \text{yr},\quad K_1+K_2=15+10=25\ \text{km/s}
\]

Thus,

\[
\frac{M_1}{M_2}
=
\frac{P_1 (K_1+K_2)_1^3}{P_2 (K_1+K_2)_2^3}
=
\frac{2 \times 15^3}{1 \times 25^3}
\approx 0.43
\]

This is closest to \(0.4\).

