Term2 = 1/[x(e^{2x}-1)].

Let y=2x. e^y -1 = y + y^2/2 + y^3/6 + y^4/24 + ...
= 2x + (4x^2)/2=2x^2 + (8x^3)/6=4/3 x^3 + (16x^4)/24=2/3 x^4 + ...
Multiply by x: x(e^{2x}-1)=2x^2 + 2x^3 + 4/3 x^4 + 2/3 x^5 + ...
= 2x^2 [1 + x + (2/3)x^2 + (1/3)x^3 + ...].
Reciprocal = 1/(2x^2) [1 - (x + 2/3 x^2 + ...) + (x + ...)^2 - ...].
Need up to constant: inside = 1 - x + [ -2/3 + 1] x^2 + ... = 1 - x + 1/3 x^2 + ...
