Now final.</think>Let the four roots be \(18,72,98,k\), and write
\[
P(x)=(x-18)(x-72)(x-98)(x-k),\qquad f(x)=\frac{P(x)}x.
\]
If the minimum is attained at two positive values \(u,v\), then \(f(u)=f(v)=m\) and \(f'(u)=f'(v)=0\). Thus \(P(x)-mx\) has double roots at \(u,v\), so
\[
P(x)-mx=(x-u)^2(x-v)^2.
\]
Comparing coefficients gives the condition
\[
T=\frac{S^2}{4}+2\sqrt V,
\]
where \(S,T,V\) are the elementary symmetric sums of the four roots.

For roots \(18,72,98,k\):
\[
S=188+k,\qquad T=10116+188k,\qquad V=127008k.
\]
So
\[
10116+188k=\frac{(188+k)^2}{4}+2\sqrt{127008k}.
\]
Let \(t=\sqrt{2k}\). Since \(\sqrt{127008}=252\sqrt2\), this becomes
\[
t^4-752t^2+8064t-20480=0.
\]
Factoring,
\[
(t-4)(t-8)(t-20)(t+32)=0.
\]
Thus positive \(t\) values are \(4,8,20\), giving
\[
k=\frac{t^2}{2}=8,32,200.
\]
Their sum is
\[
8+32+200=240.
\]

